// Snodra server protocol.
//
// A service opens one bidirectional stream per instance with Hub.Connect, announces the command
// and query types it handles with a Register message, and then exchanges Request and Reply
// messages over that stream for as long as it lives. The hub keeps an in-memory registry of
// connected instances and forwards each Request to one instance that registered its type.
//
// The hub never inspects or persists payloads. Payloads are JSON documents produced by the
// Snodra messaging libraries; the JSON shape of each type is defined by the owning service's
// *-api module (JVM) or documented contract (Rust).
